WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Three flasks.

2
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:07.120
One holds sodium chloride, one
sodium bromide, one sodium iodide.

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.380
Now the labels come off and
the flasks are shuffled.

4
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.340
They look exactly alike.

5
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:17.760
The only difference is the halide
ion: chloride, bromide or iodide.

6
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.740
So how can a few drops of just one
reagent tell the three solutions apart?

7
00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:26.840
In this mission, you'll learn why the
test starts with a little dilute acid,

8
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:29.700
and why the wrong acid would ruin it.

9
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.940
Then you'll learn a quick extra
test to settle any close calls.

10
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:39.970
Your mission: find out how a few drops of one
reagent can tell three halide solutions apart.